# StreamElements Astro probe — credentials.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this example is not.
#
# One variable per platform account. The probe opens one connection per
# variable and names it after the variable, so you can tell the connections
# apart in the log.
#
#   SE_JWT_YOUTUBE=<jwt copied while switched to the YouTube account>
#   SE_JWT_TWITCH=<jwt copied while switched to the Twitch account>
#
# Getting this wrong is harmless and worth knowing about: a token copied while
# switched to the wrong account connects fine, subscribes to the *other*
# account's room, and quietly delivers that platform's events. The probe prints
# the room and the platform each connection actually receives, so a mismatch is
# visible rather than silent.
#
# The simulator only produces events for one account at a time, so a run with
# both connections open is how you confirm both are handled at once — switch the
# active account on StreamElements between simulations and watch both keep up.
#
# SE_ROOM is optional and normally left unset: Astro resolves the room from the
# token, and the probe prints whichever room it resolved so you can check.
#
# SE_OUT=/tmp/astro.jsonl   # where to write the dump
